<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">1. Agreement to These Terms</h2>
<p>Welcome to Hello Transport. These Terms and Conditions govern your use of our website, vehicle shipping services, and transportation arrangements. By accessing our website or booking a service, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please refrain from using our services.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">2. Vehicle Shipping Arrangements</h2>
<p>Hello Transport is registered with the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration (FMCSA) under USDOT No. 4572171 and MC No. 1818817. Hello Transport arranges vehicle transportation through third-party carriers. Pickup and delivery dates are estimates based on carrier availability and scheduling, not guaranteed appointments. Transportation may be delayed by operational issues or circumstances outside our control.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">3. Booking Confirmation and Repeat Orders</h2>
<p>New customers may be required to complete and sign a booking form outlining their shipment details and agreed terms. We may retain this form for reference. For repeat bookings, we may use the information already on file, subject to confirmation of the new shipment details. Any previous agreement will apply to future orders only where its terms validly cover those orders and the customer has agreed to them.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">4. Carrier Agreements and Shipping Documents</h2>
<p>Once a carrier accepts a shipment, the carrier's bill of lading and other applicable shipping documents will govern the transportation arrangements they cover. Customers may request a copy from the carrier. If the booking agreement and carrier documents conflict, the applicable terms and the law will determine which provisions control.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">5. External Websites and Resources</h2>
<p>Our website may link to third-party websites or services. Hello Transport does not control those external platforms or their content, privacy practices, or terms. Customers should review the relevant third-party policies before sharing information or using external services.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">6. Carrier Insurance and Damage Claims</h2>
<p>The assigned carrier is generally responsible for its transportation operations and applicable cargo insurance. If your vehicle is damaged during shipment, notify the carrier and follow the claims procedure in the bill of lading and applicable insurance documents. Hello Transport will provide reasonable assistance within its role as broker, where applicable. Responsibility for any claim will be determined by the relevant agreements and applicable law.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">7. Vehicle Conditions and Excluded Damage</h2>
<p>Pre-existing mechanical problems, fluid leaks, battery or cooling-system failures, ordinary wear and tear, and damage involving loose or unsecured components may be excluded from carrier coverage, depending on the circumstances and applicable policy. This includes, for example, freezing of the engine, cooling system or battery; malfunctions of the engine, transmission, drive train, wiring, airbags, clutch or other electrical components; and wear and tear to convertible tops, mufflers and exhaust systems. Personal belongings left inside the vehicle may also be excluded. Review the carrier's insurance terms before shipping.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">8. Preparing Your Vehicle for Transport</h2>
<p>Customers must prepare their vehicles for safe transportation. Before pickup, please:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Disable alarms and anti-theft systems where appropriate.</li>
    <li>Secure or remove loose accessories, spoilers, and detachable parts.</li>
    <li>Disclose relevant mechanical issues and vehicle modifications.</li>
    <li>Remove personal belongings unless their carriage has been expressly approved.</li>
</ul>
<p>Customers may be responsible for damage caused by unsecured parts or items, including damage to other vehicles, subject to applicable law and the carrier's agreement.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">9. Rental Vehicles and Alternative Transportation</h2>
<p>Hello Transport does not automatically provide rental vehicles, replacement transportation, or reimbursement for travel expenses arising from shipping delays, accidents, damage, or unforeseen events. Any reimbursement or additional assistance must be expressly agreed upon or required by applicable law.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">10. Missed Pickup and Rescheduling Charges</h2>
<p>If a carrier arrives at the agreed pickup location and cannot collect the vehicle because it is unavailable or inaccessible, a $100 reposting fee may apply to arrange another pickup attempt. The fee and rescheduling arrangements should be confirmed with the customer before the new booking is processed.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">11. Authorized Pickup and Delivery Representatives</h2>
<p>If you cannot be present when your vehicle is collected or delivered, you must arrange for an authorized representative to act on your behalf. The representative's details should be recorded in the booking documents. Pickup or delivery notifications are generally provided approximately 3 to 24 hours in advance, depending on carrier scheduling.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">12. Payment Requirements and Delivery Arrangements</h2>
<p>Any outstanding balance must be paid according to the payment terms confirmed in your booking. Payment due at delivery must be made to the carrier in cash or by cashier's check in U.S. dollars. Customers must have the required payment available when the carrier arrives.</p>
<p>If payment cannot be completed or the delivery location is inaccessible, the carrier may arrange an alternative delivery point or terminal, where permitted. Additional transportation, storage, retrieval, or redelivery charges may apply and should be disclosed in accordance with the booking agreement and applicable law.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">13. Inoperable Vehicle Charges</h2>
<p>Vehicles that cannot operate under their own power may require special equipment or handling. A $150 non-operable vehicle fee applies when a vehicle becomes inoperable at pickup or during transportation, and is assessed at delivery. Customers should disclose the vehicle's condition before booking and confirm any applicable charges in writing.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">14. Personal Belongings and Liability</h2>
<p>Unless expressly approved in advance, vehicles, including the trunk, should be transported without personal belongings. Hello Transport and the carrier may not accept responsibility for items left inside the vehicle, subject to applicable law and the specific circumstances. Liability for vehicle damage will depend on the applicable agreements, insurance coverage, and legal requirements.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">15. Documenting Vehicle Damage</h2>
<p>Customers should document the vehicle's condition before pickup and again at delivery. Any newly discovered damage should be recorded on the applicable inspection report or bill of lading before signing, where possible. Keep copies of inspection records, photographs, and shipping documents to support any subsequent claim. Claims must follow the carrier's applicable procedures and deadlines.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">16. Applicable Law and Legal Proceedings</h2>
<p>Legal claims arising from these terms are to be filed in Baltimore County, Maryland. Any venue requirement is subject to applicable law and cannot override mandatory legal rights.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">17. Order Cancellation and Refunds</h2>
<p>Cancellation requests must be submitted in writing through an accepted communication method, such as email. The following fees and refunds apply:</p>
<ul>
    <li>$99 cancellation fee if cancellation occurs before a carrier is assigned.</li>
    <li>$199 cancellation fee if a carrier has already been assigned.</li>
    <li>A full deposit refund if the vehicle has not been scheduled for pickup within 30 days of the initial available date.</li>
</ul>
<p>Customers should receive written confirmation of any applicable fee or refund.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">18. Service Refusal and Order Termination</h2>
<p>Hello Transport may decline or terminate a booking where permitted by law, including when a customer breaches the agreement, provides materially inaccurate information, or engages in threatening or abusive conduct. Any cancellation charges and deposit refunds will be handled according to the booking terms and applicable law.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">19. Transportation Service Disclaimer</h2>
<p>Hello Transport arranges transportation through third-party carriers and does not directly control every aspect of their operations. Pickup and delivery estimates may change due to carrier schedules, traffic, weather, mechanical problems, or other circumstances. We will communicate material updates when reasonably possible. Carrier performance and damage claims are addressed under the relevant carrier agreement and applicable law.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">20. Limits on Responsibility</h2>
<p>To the extent permitted by law, Hello Transport is not responsible for losses caused solely by circumstances outside its control or by independent third parties for whom it is not legally responsible. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limits any non-waivable consumer rights.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">21. Revisions to These Terms</h2>
<p>Hello Transport may update these Terms and Conditions when business practices, services, or legal requirements change. The latest version will be published on this page with an updated revision date. Changes will apply as permitted by law, and customers will be informed when required. Continuing to use our services after an update is published means you accept the revised terms, to the extent permitted by law.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">22. Events Beyond Reasonable Control</h2>
<p>Hello Transport may be unable to perform or arrange services on schedule because of events beyond reasonable control, including severe weather, natural disasters, public emergencies, strikes, government restrictions, or other significant disruptions. We will make reasonable efforts to communicate relevant delays and help arrange a revised schedule when circumstances permit.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">23. Personal Information and Privacy</h2>
<p>We collect and use customer information as described in our <a class="ht-pp-link" href="{{ route('Frontend.privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a>. We do not sell or rent your personal information. Relevant details may be shared with carriers and service providers when necessary to arrange transportation or complete a requested transaction. Please review our Privacy Policy for further information about data collection, use, disclosure, and privacy choices.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">24. Vehicle Condition Inspections</h2>
<p>Customers should inspect and document existing vehicle damage before transportation. The assigned carrier may also conduct a pickup inspection. At delivery, the customer or authorized representative should examine the vehicle and record any apparent new damage on the delivery inspection report before signing, where possible. Photographs and signed inspection documents may help establish the vehicle's condition. Any damage claim must follow the carrier's procedures, applicable deadlines, and governing law. Failure to record damage may affect a claim but does not automatically eliminate rights that cannot legally be waived.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">25. Resolving Customer Disputes</h2>
<p>If a disagreement arises, the customer and Hello Transport should first attempt to resolve it through direct communication. Where appropriate and agreed upon, the parties may pursue mediation with a neutral third party.</p>
<p>If mediation is unsuccessful, the dispute may be resolved through binding arbitration under the rules of the American Arbitration Association (AAA), subject to applicable law and any legal rights that cannot be waived.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">26. Additional Charges for Difficult Locations</h2>
<p>Deliveries to remote areas, restricted-access communities, rural roads, mountainous regions, or locations that cannot accommodate the carrier's equipment may require alternative arrangements or additional charges. Any additional fee must be communicated to the customer and agreed upon in writing before the affected service is performed.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">27. Vehicle Acceptance Requirements</h2>
<p>Some vehicles may be unsuitable for a particular carrier because of their size, weight, modifications, condition, or equipment requirements. Hello Transport may decline a shipment if safe and lawful transportation cannot be arranged. If a vehicle is determined to be ineligible after booking, any applicable refund will be handled according to the booking agreement and applicable law.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">28. Ownership and Required Vehicle Documents</h2>
<p>Customers must have legal ownership of the vehicle or proper authorization to arrange its transportation. Hello Transport or the assigned carrier may request relevant documentation, such as registration, title, or other proof of authorization, where necessary.</p>
<p>Customers are responsible for providing accurate information and resolving ownership disputes or documentation issues within their control. Transportation may be declined if required documents are unavailable or legal authorization cannot be established.</p>

<h2 class="ht-section-title-2">29. Age Requirement</h2>
<p>You must be at least 18 years of age to register, sign up, or enter into any agreement with Hello Transport.</p>

